  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Fedora already works with Java 6, but we are considering discontinuing support for Java 5 for several reasons:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "1) As of Nov 3, 2009, J2SE 5 has reached its End Of Service Life (EOSL).  This means there will be no more public updates to Sun's J2SE 5.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2) Finding and installing Java 5 on the various operating systems is becoming increasingly difficult.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "3) Java 6 has several API and annotation improvements we'd like to be able to take advantage of in the source code.  (For example, IOException now has a constructor that accepts a Throable cause, and @Override can now apply to interface method implementations)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For now, this would also reduce the number of different configurations we'd need to test prior to release, thus shortening the release cycle.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In early January 2010, the committers agreed that this is the direction we want to go, but we should first poll our users to see what, if any, problems this might create for them.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Upon deciding to move to Java 6, the following changes should be made immediately:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "A) Change the pom to compile to java 6 bytecode (and thus require a Java 6 JDK)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "B) Remove the JDBC3/4 code-rewriting hack in the build",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "C) Modify the CI tests to run using Java 6",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
