      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I sent out a survey to the fedora-users list in early January.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"http://www.surveymonkey.com/s/DLRSFF5\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.surveymonkey.com/s/DLRSFF5</a></p>\n\n<p>This survey was open for a week.  Here are the final results:</p>\n\n<p>31 people took the survey.</p>\n\n<p>Q1: Which of the following apply to you?</p>\n\n<p>24 (77%) use Fedora in production<br/>\n28 (90%) develop software that uses the SOAP/REST apis.<br/>\n16 (52%) develop software that uses Fedora's Java interfaces.<br/>\n3 (10%) are Fedora committers</p>\n\n<p>Q2: Which app server(s) do you deploy with?</p>\n\n<p>17 (55%) deploy with the bundled version of Tomcat<br/>\n9 deploy with a non-bundled Tomcat 6.x (1 of those said they were moving toward JBoss)<br/>\n5 deploy with a non-bundled Tomcat 5.5<br/>\n4 deploy with a non-bundled Tomcat but did not specify a version</p>\n\n<p>Q3: Which version of Java do you run Fedora with?</p>\n\n<p>12 (39%) said Java 5<br/>\n25 (81%) said Java 6</p>\n\n<p>Q4: Do you foresee a problem if future versions of Fedora require Java 6?</p>\n\n<p>30 (97%) said no<br/>\n1 (3%) said yes, \"My App Server is not Java 6 compatible\", but this person also said they were only deploying with the bundled version of Tomcat (which is Java 6 compatible), and declined to provide contact information.</p>",
     "created": "11/Jan/10 3:44 PM",
